# Review

The title makes a contestable claim about what readers can do when following links. A reader could reasonably argue that the prose around a link can supply the premise even when the linked note has a topical title. The note gives a concrete reason to prefer a claim title in some cases. An inline link introduced by “because” can state the premise in the link text itself, so the reader can see how it supports the argument before opening the note. The title’s main verb asserts that effect of the naming convention.
